# Project rules

- Project name is **File Processing**.
- Keep `app/main.py` thin: application assembly and lifecycle only.
- Place HTTP route handlers under `app/api/routes/` and use `APIRouter`.
- Place SQLAlchemy ORM models under `app/models/` and database configuration/sessions under `app/db/`.
- Place Pydantic API contracts under `app/schemas/`.
- Place business logic, file parsing, persistence and exports under `app/services/`.
- Use dependency-injected SQLAlchemy sessions in route handlers, not module-global request sessions.
- Persist both original uploaded bytes and parsed records/PDF text in the database for the MVP; plan object storage for production binaries.
- Maintain compatibility with existing `/api/v1/files/*` endpoints.
- Add tests covering file processing and database persistence. Run `python -m pytest -q`.
- Never commit `storage/`, uploaded files, SQLite databases, `.env` or credentials.
- Treat the current API as local-only, unauthenticated and not production secure.
- Prefer focused PRs; do not merge or force-push to `main` without review.
